#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531695} :activity/id #uuid "dd92c948-0eff-59d9-8a07-30fdc5ab0737" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050993 :topic/id #uuid "77b8e530-6866-509a-8397-d35f1b4f5874" :topic/math-academy-id 2097} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531678 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360775 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3859bb5-c8b9-50e8-8eef-3af0c8937ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452353} {:answer/id #uuid "da6c7dee-677d-5806-85b1-6f0588358ddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452354}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452354} :answer-field/id #uuid "eca96214-aff5-5f05-ada1-12ce791f90fc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453024} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d6b082d-2576-5e1d-8655-c6e913dd6e9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452355} {:answer/id #uuid "44335011-eb8f-5a0b-bb95-f537858c1e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452356}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452356} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f9df55b-6d6a-5739-9911-e251543e8b83" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453025} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edba4c44-368b-51d4-98cb-48bf0ea196b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452357} {:answer/id #uuid "fdbde816-1bd9-5b75-8fc3-21d0b2f05e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452358}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452357} :answer-field/id #uuid "7767b767-280a-5089-ad8f-b2a80f87660b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453026}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0d89a9f6-d33c-56fa-8ee8-b25b137af49f" :question/math-academy-id "q-97264" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **II.** $⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$\n- **III.** $⟨a,a⟩>0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is true. By the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument, we have \n\n$$\n⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=\\overset{―}{(\\overset{―}{\\alpha })}⟨a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that if $a=0$ then $⟨a,a⟩=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "2b42f750-9a7e-5f8b-a758-4b09386e27b9" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531713}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531695 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360770 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "009f944f-2564-5ff8-be03-409e2921e773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5+2\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357758} {:answer/id #uuid "07d2de99-134c-56ed-a01e-3888e44a2e43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5-3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357821} {:answer/id #uuid "3515590e-583b-5005-bda7-1d033ecdb5de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2+5\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358228} {:answer/id #uuid "514d82ec-bdd1-5145-ab0a-ca3efb7d0dbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358450} {:answer/id #uuid "7da5eed9-1a74-5728-973a-3fd547d58c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358846}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358228} :answer-field/id #uuid "a251cdec-b884-550f-9109-86fd04483762" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0821bac1-cf18-5c7e-985e-332add7238bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-97209" :question/problem "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨4a-b,\\,c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨c,a⟩=1-2\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨b,c⟩=2+3\\text{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨4a-b,\\,c⟩ & =⟨4a,c⟩-⟨b,c⟩ \\\\  & =4⟨a,c⟩-⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4⟨a,c⟩-⟨b,c⟩ & =4\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}-⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨c,a⟩$ and $⟨b,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}-⟨b,c⟩ & =4\\overset{―}{(1-2\\text{i})}-(2+3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =4(1+2\\text{i})-(2+3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =4+8\\text{i}-2-3\\text{i} \\\\  & =2+5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7a2f8e3c-95b7-5e85-817c-a0d82602286a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531678}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531710 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "192a18d2-9632-54a2-8edf-f7f1746b01ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7-4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269479} {:answer/id #uuid "3af73c1a-1981-593b-9ed2-36c5f9f11501" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8+7\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269805} {:answer/id #uuid "cb97711c-ab2a-500c-97a3-13e99ff1a5e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7+4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271057} {:answer/id #uuid "e210d3b6-fd4f-52ce-8a13-7413118300ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8+\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271255} {:answer/id #uuid "f541938c-a1cd-59ed-b973-017084b179c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7+8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271422}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271422} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2bc77b2-cd0a-5d4a-99e1-6259be28d214" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6190711d-7ba0-5244-bc34-0cc4e9ad3523" :question/math-academy-id "q-141161" :question/problem "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨2a+3b,\\,c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨c,a⟩=2-\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨b,c⟩=1+2\\text{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨2a+3b,\\,c⟩ & =⟨2a,c⟩+⟨3b,c⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨a,c⟩+3⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2⟨a,c⟩+3⟨b,c⟩ & =2\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}+3⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨c,a⟩$ and $⟨b,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}+3⟨b,c⟩ & =2(\\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}})+3(1+2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2(2+\\text{i})+3(1+2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =4+2\\text{i}+3+6\\text{i} \\\\  & =7+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b58576dc-b950-5cb9-94db-ca8f23e36cbe"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531711 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360784 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc8dac23-f647-5deb-86a4-621fd31c1d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452383} {:answer/id #uuid "6e03bff6-a5ff-50e6-9218-131abe220023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452384}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452384} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e9c2f28-e2b4-59be-ae0d-5cc27032c71a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453039} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30d384c3-9e31-5d82-9ef2-635c223f8ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452385} {:answer/id #uuid "140655d4-6272-5a39-a781-b9c1417ede63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452386}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452385} :answer-field/id #uuid "e50118f5-3a96-5d52-9890-18e710ce477d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453040} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1709b99a-c168-519e-a774-35d4b3d2341e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452387} {:answer/id #uuid "f478c422-93f8-5410-a67c-fea2ce11d298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452388}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452388} :answer-field/id #uuid "86902f25-2bcd-545b-9255-65d88893b5e5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8247f7d2-00cd-54b9-9bd1-43c13383de3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-97303" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨b,a⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨a,b⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **II.** $i⟨a,b⟩=⟨-ia,b⟩$ for any  $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- **III.** $⟨a,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is false. A complex  inner product is linear  in the first argument,  so we have \n\n$$\n⟨-ia,b⟩=-i⟨a,b⟩\\ne i⟨a,b⟩,\n$$\n\nin general.\n\n- Statement III is true. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$  $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "b9c2039c-a815-5440-94dd-50c9bbba18a0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531710}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531713 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360783 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9be7f699-9974-5201-8e47-accce63d5602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452377} {:answer/id #uuid "19455cdc-333a-5561-bab6-00ec79218d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452378}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452377} :answer-field/id #uuid "5582b199-c5bf-5709-9377-1286b2173eaa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453036} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d491e753-0d53-5704-b768-2cde723d0d30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452379} {:answer/id #uuid "fda07ff9-ba7b-5689-857e-ab9f1cd84952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452380}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452380} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3df9eb2-97cb-5280-9fe0-ea7eec6cc287" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453037} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d1794a0-b828-5e06-b8cc-54a54ad72949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452381} {:answer/id #uuid "b15deefa-87b8-5a6a-89b0-4f57df04b649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452382}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186452381} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b86e18f-b4ac-528d-b5e3-1bc836241d7d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "354bca31-ea8a-5e1d-a896-d3e34e677d11" :question/math-academy-id "q-97296" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨a,b⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n\n- **II.** $i⟨a,b⟩=⟨a,-ib⟩$ for any  $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n\n- **III.** There is vector $a\\in {C}^{n}$ such that  $⟨a,a⟩<0$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. A complex number is equal to its conjugate if and only if it is a real number. The inner product over $C$  is a complex number in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument, we have \n\n$$\n⟨a,-ib⟩=\\overset{―}{(-i)}⟨a,b⟩=i⟨a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false.  The inner product over $C$ is positive-definite. So, for any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩\\ge 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "ba88a8d8-f925-5c60-9a9e-df08b26bbbfb" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531711}}] :activity/title "The Inner Product in Vector Spaces Over the Complex Numbers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530864}]}
